{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show bbd7564:packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts | nl -ba'","aggregated_output":"     1\t/**\n     2\t * Renders a tooltip model as text (spec I1, DX8: textContent only), in one of two presentations decided by\n     3\t * the controller's layout (decision 0004 revision 3, rule 5): floating, placed by `placement.ts`, or as\n     4\t * running text in the strip reserved under the plot.\n     5\t *\n     6\t * - A hovered tooltip is text, takes no pointer events and is hidden from assistive technology: the plot's\n     7\t *   keyboard proxy carries the same reading, so nothing is said twice and nothing here is a live region (A7).\n     8\t * - A pinned tooltip or strip takes events and is exposed (rule 9): its rows are buttons named by their text,\n     9\t *   at least 24 × 24 CSS px, outside the tab order (the closed chart keeps its two tab stops; the keyboard\n    10\t *   reaches the same series through the plot's own Up and Down). Its \"+N more\" is a button too, showing the\n    11\t *   next rows, so every row can be chosen by pointer.\n    12\t * - Rows keep their element across redraws while their identity (series, datum) is unchanged, and nodes\n    13\t *   are only moved when their order changes, so a press that spans a data update still completes.\n    14\t * - Floating: rows are dropped from the end into \"+N more\" until a candidate is valid (rule 6); the tooltip\n    15\t *   is never larger than the visible part of the plot; with one row and still nothing valid, the last resort\n    16\t *   of rule 6 is used, and when even that would cover a control or a focus ring nothing floats.\n    17\t * - Strip: at least the x and one row are always shown.\n    18\t */\n    19\timport type { DatumText, Rect, TooltipModel } from '../core/contracts';\n    20\timport { createSwatch, type SwatchSpec } from './swatch';\n    21\timport { fallbackPlacement, placeTool