{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show bbd7564:docs/decisions/0003-default-palette.md | rg -n 'surround|5.89|14.43|3:1'\"","aggregated_output":"16:Spec: A5 (palette thresholds, provisional), L2 (3:1 for marks), F9 (eight series). Finding R7, docs/01-landscape.md.\n163:- **Dark.** `#e3e8f0` is under 3:1 against five dark series colors: blue 2.27, orange 2.54, green 1.17, cyan 1.58 and pink 1.96. Purple (4.70), red (4.04) and slate (3.94) pass. No single ink reaches 3:1 against both `#16181d` and the light green; even white reaches only 1.44:1 against it.\n166:A datum outline crossing a mark therefore fails WCAG 1.4.11 wherever it is drawn in one ink. The chart core is changing the indicator to two tones: a ring in the focus token, with a surround in the background color between the ring and the marks. That work is not in my files.\n170:1. **The focus color must reach 3:1 against the background.** The ring is seen against its surround, which is the background color. Light `#1f5fcc` on `#ffffff` is 5.89:1; dark `#e3e8f0` on `#16181d` is 14.43:1. Both pass, and the L2 token test asserts it.\n171:2. **The surround must reach 3:1 against every mark it touches.** That is constraint 1 read the other way: every series color reaches 3:1 on its background (lowest 3.10 light, 3.07 dark), and so do the axis and reference tokens. Nothing new is needed.\n172:3. **The focus color needs no contrast against series colors.** The surround keeps them from touching.\n279:- **Spread.** Light L ran from 0.43 to 0.68. Three colors (green, purple and magenta, at L 0.43–0.49) were much darker than the three near 3:1.\n294:   - From random starts it found feasible light sets only once the boxes were split into tiers: blue, orange and slate near 3:1, red and cyan in the middle, green, purple and magenta lower (`configs/tier-44-free.json`).\n354:| Scheme | Below 3:1 on white | Min ΔE normal / protan / deutan / tritan (closes