{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_107","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show bbd7564:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core-final.interaction.review.md | nl -ba | sed -n '33,69p' | sed -E 's@/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/@@g'\"","aggregated_output":"    33\t|---|---|---|\n    34\t| C2-1 · B · Paused call order | **Fixed** | **Trace.** Pause → append A → replace with B → append C → Resume. Accepted replacement clears the old held frame. Rejected replacement preserves it, and paused append validates before publishing. I6. [controller.ts:605](src/core/controller.ts:605) |\n    35\t| C2-2 · B · Category identity | **Fixed for the reported slide** | **Trace.** On `A,B,C → B,C,D`, focused B follows B, focused A moves to B, and a pin or dismissal on A ends. A transition with no surviving focus still needs the recovery in #2. A3, A7. [interaction.ts:1501](src/dom/interaction.ts:1501) |\n    36\t| C2-3 · B · Empty-window recovery | **Fixed with a new defect** | **Node + trace.** Empty zoom retains `0`, Zoom out and Reset. Loading is distinguished from empty, Resume is available, and all-zero slices can be listed with the table disabled. Reset can leave stale focus, and the new slice actions lack keyboard access. #2–3. I3, I6, L7. [interaction.ts:405](src/dom/interaction.ts:405) |\n    37\t| C2-4 · B · Frozen native range | **Fixed** | **Trace.** Focus a one-point chart and append. The native maximum and ordinal are synchronized independently of the text guard. The remaining state-text and translation defects are #2 and #14. A3, A7. [interaction.ts:602](src/dom/interaction.ts:602) |\n    38\t| C2-5 · M · Retained revisions and caller rows | **Fixed for the reported path** | **Trace.** With displayed A, accepted B and a later paused append, retirement accounts separately for the on-screen and pending frame. It freezes the on-screen row source before advancing its retirement floor. I did not measure memory. I6, plan §1.5. [controller.ts:1348](src/core/controller.ts:1348) |\n    39\t| C2-6 · M · Native range intent | **Fixed** | **Trace.** Home at the first point leaves no pending direction. `input` and `change` resolve the absolute ordinal, duplicate notifications are guarded, and focus takeover reads the pointer datum first. A2, A3. [interaction.ts:763](src/dom/interaction.ts:763) |\n    40\t| C2-7 · M · Keyboard information loss | **Partly fixed** | **Node + trace.** Hidden-only x positions, ordinary totals, narrowed scatter steps and the full coincidence count are accounted for. With ten stacked series and one gap, I still got **three** `incomplete` qualifications, on S8, S9 and the total. Format the overflow series from unqualified row values and qualify the total once. I1, A3, §3.6. [focus.ts:133](src/core/focus.ts:133) · [aligned.ts:57](src/lookup/aligned.ts:57) |\n    41\t| C2-8 · M · Single-pointer pan and selection | **Partly fixed** | **Node + trace.** Tap selects, and pan buttons exist. From `[25,75]` in `[0,100]`, keyboard pan gave `[30,80]`, button pan `[50,100]`. Tap never assigns the `focus` used by Zoom in. Arbitrary drag endpoints and overflow row selections still lack equivalent controls. Retain the touch anchor and offer start/end clicks or fields for exact range selection. I3, I4, WCAG 2.5.7. [interaction.ts:1152](src/dom/interaction.ts:1152) · [interaction.ts:1388](src/dom/interaction.ts:1388) |\n    42\t| C2-9 · M · Unattainable zoom minimum | **Fixed for the reported cases** | **Node.** Two or three positions over `[0,100]` halve, and `[10¹⁶,10¹⁶+4]` narrows to a representable width of 2. Under the amended matrix, category line, area and bar all exclude zoom. I3, §3.6. [focus.ts:381](src/core/focus.ts:381) |\n    43\t| C2-10 · M · Gesture ownership and cancellation | **Fixed** | **Trace.** Escape releases a captured drag. Pinch retains its original two IDs, cancellation drops queued work, ordinary lift keeps the final queued move, and the remaining finger cannot become a tap. The horizontal midpoint uses the upward scale direction. I3, I4. [interaction.ts:1077](src/dom/interaction.ts:1077) · [interaction.ts:1208](src/dom/interaction.ts:1208) |\n    44\t| C2-11 · M · Stale scatter pin | **Partly fixed** | **Node + trace.** Pin `(5,100)` and restrict y to `[0,10]`: the missing anchor ends the pin. Newly coincident rows are re-picked. The originally pinned ref can still be replaced by another group member. Fix #9. I1, A7. [interaction.ts:1528](src/dom/interaction.ts:1528) |\n    45\t| C2-12 · M · Clipped or transformed tooltip | **Partly fixed** | **Node + trace.** Simple positive scaling and pinned/keyboard scroll repositioning are present. Overwide fallback, ancestor clipping, and nontrivial transforms remain. Fix #4 and #13. I1, A2, A6. [tooltip.ts:221](src/dom/tooltip.ts:221) |\n    46\t| C2-13 · M · Narrow readout | **Partly fixed** | **Trace.** The strip occupies its own flow space, and a displayed pinned row can receive a click. Approaching it can still change or lose the datum. Fix #5 and #12. I1, I4, WCAG 1.4.13. [interaction.ts:1007](src/dom/interaction.ts:1007) |\n    47\t| C2-14 · M · Invisible arcless focus | **Fixed for the reported mixed donut** | **Trace.** With zero followed by a positive slice, the plot outline is inset and the current zero slice has a visible list outline. The all-zero action case is #3. F8, A2. [interaction.ts:573](src/dom/interaction.ts:573) · [css.ts:250](src/theme/css.ts:250) |\n    48\t| C2-15 · M · Open-table layout | **Fixed for the reported cases** | **Trace.** Open a table, move the legend right and shrink the card. The table is positioned in the responsive plot column. Its scroll region flexes and the disclosure stays outside the overlay. A4, A6. [interaction.ts:1354](src/dom/interaction.ts:1354) · [css.ts:290](src/theme/css.ts:290) |\n    49\t| C2-16 · M · Unrequested page-count announcement | **Fixed at the DOM level** | **Trace.** Append row 201 with page one open. The status switches to `aria-live=\"off\"` before changing the count. Reader paging enables polite updates. A7. [table.ts:144](src/dom/table.ts:144) |\n    50\t| C2-17 · M · Focus lost on removal or reorder | **Partly fixed** | **Trace.** Reordering a surviving button restores it, and collapsing the pager transfers focus to the scroll region. Change to compact with the toolbar or table field focused: `handOff` handles only the proxy, and teardown can then remove the destination control. Hand off focus from any disappearing chart-owned subtree. A2, A4, WCAG 2.4.3. [interaction.ts:340](src/dom/interaction.ts:340) · [interaction.ts:369](src/dom/interaction.ts:369) |\n    51\t| C2-18 · M · Jump-to input | **Partly fixed** | **Trace.** Exact ordinary categories, common grouped numbers and associated visible errors improved. `12garbage` is accepted as 12, the number grammar assumes ASCII digits and three-digit groups, and the displayed wall-time fallback returns only the date. Parse the actual field format, locale and unit, preserve wall time, and reject extraneous text. A4, WCAG 3.3.1. [interaction.ts:1266](src/dom/interaction.ts:1266) · [interaction.ts:1294](src/dom/interaction.ts:1294) |\n    52\t| C2-19 · M · Language and replaceable text | **Partly fixed** | **Trace.** Plot instructions, point templates, note runs and default summary language exist. On a German page, translating just `plotLabel` removes English marking from the remaining English role/value. Table cells and donut missing-value text also lack per-string marking. Put names and descriptions on appropriately tagged text elements and carry language to generated cells and runs. A3, A10, WCAG 3.1.2. [interaction.ts:1483](src/dom/interaction.ts:1483) · [table.ts:124](src/dom/table.ts:124) |\n    53\t| C2-20 · M · Stale axis unit | **Fixed** | **Node.** Changing only the second series from `ms` to `s` changes the effective shared title and layout key. L6. [focus2.test.ts:138](test/core/focus2.test.ts:138) |\n    54\t| C2-21 · M · Accessibility evidence | **Partly fixed** | **Trace.** The acceptance suite checks real focus, role, painted ring geometry and more state preconditions. The point text still comes from the DOM, pinned actions lack a positive AX assertion, the five rehearsals are absent, and the published A9 page is a placeholder. Publish the criterion-to-test/author-obligation table with its test-existence check and identify the manual evidence gap. A2, A3, A7–A9. [Acceptance ring check](test/browser/acceptance/a2-keyboard.browser.test.ts:256) · [Conformance page](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/pages/conformance.md:3) |\n    55\t| C2-22 · m · Contrast dash in swatches | **Fixed** | **Trace.** Switch to increased contrast or forced colors. The line swatch carries both dash patterns and CSS selects the contrast pattern. A5, F9. [swatch.ts:103](src/dom/swatch.ts:103) |\n    56\t| C3-1 · B · Narrowed scatter hangs | **Fixed** | **Trace.** For `A0,B1,A2,B3,A4`, an absolute adjustment to ordinal 2 uses bounded global steps and leaves narrowed mode when it reaches A2. There is a synthetic regression for exactly this input. A2, A3. [interaction.ts:684](src/dom/interaction.ts:684) · [review3 test](test/browser/chart/review3.browser.test.ts:27) |\n    57\t| C3-2 · B · Table covers right toolbar | **Fixed** | **Trace.** Open View as table with `legend:'right'`. Focus enters the scroll region and the disclosure remains in the adjacent column. A2, A4, WCAG 2.4.11. [interaction.ts:1309](src/dom/interaction.ts:1309) |\n    58\t| C3-3 · M · Pointer-speed-dependent tooltip | **Fixed with a new defect** | **Trace.** The old tooltip no longer follows the pointer or intercepts a hovered click. Coordinate-based holding can nevertheless select the old datum, and a required hover route can fail. Fix #1, #5 and #8. I1, I4. [interaction.ts:872](src/dom/interaction.ts:872) |\n    59\t| C3-4 · M · Focused streaming text churn | **Partly fixed** | **Node + trace.** Default position-only changes can stay silent at the attribute level. Translated position syntax defeats the comparison. Fix #14. A7, A10. [interaction.ts:607](src/dom/interaction.ts:607) |\n    60\t| C3-5 · M · Replacement splits text and focus | **Fixed for epoch replacement** | **Trace.** Replace the data while keyboard-focused. The epoch branch clears old presentation identity and stores the new effective focus before writing. Same-epoch recovery still needs #2. A2, A3. [interaction.ts:1552](src/dom/interaction.ts:1552) |\n    61\t| C3-6 · M · Compact or too-small transition | **Partly fixed** | **Trace.** A focused proxy hands off, and compact preparation clears the old overlay before dropping the frame. Other focused subtrees can be removed, and `clear()` leaves the corridor, held rectangle and rest state. Apply C2-17 and #8 on every rebuild. A2, C1. [interaction.ts:1605](src/dom/interaction.ts:1605) · [interaction.ts:1630](src/dom/interaction.ts:1630) |\n    62\t| C3-7 · M · Zoom-in widens | **Fixed for the reported key/wheel path** | **Node + trace.** `+` on public window `[40,45]` with minimum 20 produces no widening. Pinch still has its own arithmetic: spreading the fingers from that window can impose width 20. Apply the same directional guard to pinch. I3, I4. [focus.ts:352](src/core/focus.ts:352) · [interaction.ts:1209](src/dom/interaction.ts:1209) |\n    63\t| C3-8 · M · Misleading unavailable slider | **Fixed with a new defect** | **Trace.** Loading cannot masquerade as an empty zoom. Hiding every series sets a one-position range and leaves legend recovery. Recovery of the actual datum/text cache is incomplete as in #2. L7, A2, A3. [interaction.ts:594](src/dom/interaction.ts:594) |\n    64\t| C3-9 · M · Unusable touch targets | **Partly fixed** | **Trace.** Displayed pin rows and slice-list choices have 24 px minima, and opening the table closes a pin. Truncated rows lack selection, pinned buttons are AX-hidden, and an all-zero list lacks keyboard access. Fix #3, #6 and #7. I4, A2, F8. [css.ts:197](src/theme/css.ts:197) |\n    65\t| C3-10 · M · Gesture work crosses owners | **Fixed for the reported sequences** | **Trace.** Blur, detach, cancellation and teardown cancel pending pinch work. A third finger cannot substitute into the active pair, and a nonzoomable mouse press is captured through release. I3, I4. [interaction.ts:349](src/dom/interaction.ts:349) · [interaction.ts:1065](src/dom/interaction.ts:1065) |\n    66\t| C3-11 · M · Bar cue repeats at 33 | **Fixed by specification amendment** | **Trace.** Series 9 and 33 still repeat. Current F9 explicitly permits repetition beyond 32, and acceptance checks all 32 combinations. No implementation change is required for this finding. [Spec F9](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/02-product-spec.md:102) · [32-series test](test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:550) |\n    67\t\n    68\t## Decision 0004 revision 2\n    69\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
