{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_130","type":"agent_message","text":"**No. At `bbd7564`, the original held-mouse-click and empty-window-reset blockers are fixed. A pin can still switch to a different series, a redraw can strand a pressed row, and a focused category can be announced again solely because its ordinal changed.**\n\nI read the committed blobs with `git show bbd7564:<path>`. I ran six committed Node suites in memory using Node’s test runner, Vitest assertions, and fast-check. No files changed. Browser behavior below is a source trace unless identified as a Node result.\n\n## Findings from the final review\n\nSeverity is the original review’s **B** blocker, **M** major, or **m** minor. Source filenames are under `packages/axylo/src`. Browser test names below give the file stem, line, and identifying part of the test title. A named test covers the stated case. **None** identifies a missing regression test.\n\n| Finding | Severity | Status | Evidence at `bbd7564` | Reverting test |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 · Held mouse click | B | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:1222,1232` picks the mouse-release coordinates independently of `held`. | `final-hold:43` “Q4’s exact datum and row”, `:61` “a click selects B”, `:93` “empty hole selects nothing” |\n| 2 · Empty-window reset | B | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:805,1748,1797` clears the state-text cache and establishes focus before writing or drawing. | `final-pin:26` “focus, reading, ring, tooltip and Enter agree on x 0” |\n| 3 · All-zero donut actions | B | **fixed with a new defect** | `interaction.ts:216,257,267` gives the list one stop and native activation. Replacing its entries can drop focus at `:264`. | `final-pin:53` “Tab reaches the slice list”; **none** for a focused list redraw |\n| 4 · Placement and clipping | B | **partly fixed** | `placement.ts:98,144,169` shifts around supplied obstacles and rejects oversize boxes. `interaction.ts:755,765` supplies incomplete clipping and focus obstacles. | `focus-placement:47,58,64,102` control shift, clipped alignment, overwidth, fallback; **none** for the omitted geometry below |\n| 5 · Hoverable route | B | **fixed with a new defect** | `interaction.ts:483,1084` and `placement.ts:209` give all placements the same rested route. A stationary pointer does not start a new rest when a commit changes its datum at `interaction.ts:1778`. | `final-hold:119,139,156,172` dense edge, horizontal strip, scatter strip, no-rest converse; **none** for rest interrupted by a frame |\n| 6 · Accessible and selectable pin rows | M | **partly fixed** | `tooltip.ts:125,198,220` exposes named buttons and paging. `focus.ts:171` can omit actual group members. `tooltip.ts:356` can leave the only row or paging button clipped. | `final-pin:115` named AX buttons, `:153` ten exact coincidences, `:182` secondary strip tap; **none** for interrupted group order or a clipped last action |\n| 7 · Press across redraw | M | **partly fixed** | `tooltip.ts:153` reuses a row in the same presentation. Its aligned key includes formatted text at `:75`. Switching presentation discards the node at `:248,257`. | `final-pin:133` “secondary row held across an append”; **none** for reordering, reformatting, or crossing the strip threshold during a press |\n| 8 · Hold outlives geometry | M | **partly fixed** | `interaction.ts:1770,1803` re-picks after ordinary geometry changes. `:319` ignores sub-half-pixel changes, and `:1829` drops a held presentation without clearing its rest. | `final-hold:187` “Q4 at once, without a move”; `:206` only excludes Q3 after resize |\n| 9 · Pin and dismissal identity | M | **partly fixed** | `interaction.ts:1688` checks the original scatter ref. Escape uses the group’s current first ref at `:1365`, and `pointer.ts:41` searches only the capped sample. Aligned pins replace their ref at `interaction.ts:1698`. | `final-pin:222,241` hide pinned A and dismiss A before adding B; **none** for reversed operation order, sample overflow, or hidden aligned A |\n| 10 · Wrong focus geometry | M | **fixed** for the reported datum ring and single-series union | `interaction.ts:691,745,762` independently supplies the keyboard ring and the union of displayed marks. `focus.ts:344,370` uses the same ring geometry for painting and exclusion. | `final-pin:258` “covers neither series’ point”; `focus-placement:73` “keyboard ring elsewhere”. **None** for omitting that ring at the DOM call site while hovering B. |\n| 11 · Donut hole | M | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:750` supplies both scaled radii after clearance. `placement.ts:131` tests the farthest corners and the ring strokes before the other candidates. | `focus-placement:121,127,133` oversized tip, fitting tip in an enclosing slice box, crossing stroke |\n| 12 · Short plots | M | **partly fixed** | `controller.ts:1323` selects three modes, and `css.ts:192` reserves two strip line heights. The initial eligibility calculation still uses the plot text’s estimated height at `controller.ts:1316`. | `final-review.test.ts:255,265` “92 px plot” and “keeps 80 px”; `final-hold:380` “never a floating tooltip”. **None** for an actual strip height different from the estimate. |\n| 13 · Transformed ancestors | M | **partly fixed** | `mapping.ts:47,65,69` uses fractional, independent scales. `chart.ts:196` retains the **known** measurement issue. The promised transform limit is absent from spec §3.8 at `02-product-spec.md:214`. | `final-pin:315` painted bar centres under `scale(1.015)` and translated nonuniform scale, SVG only. **None** there for physical layout extent. |\n| 14 · Translated range text | M | **fixed with a new defect** | `focus.ts:196` removes dependence on translated position syntax. The single-series key at `:206` includes a category’s changing numeric index. | `final-pin:81` translated `pointOf`; **none** for an unchanged, narrowed category sliding to another ordinal |\n| 15 · One Escape | M | **fixed with a new defect** | `interaction.ts:1353` spends a visible tooltip’s Escape before the proxy or dialog. `:1363` lets Escape through when a pin exists but its content is hidden. | `final-hold:264,301` three Escapes in a dialog and page listener; **none** for an invisible pin |\n| 16 · `tooltip:false` invisible pin | M | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:157,1247` prevents pin entry; mouse focus and selection still run at `:1248,1257`. | `final-hold:323` “click A, move over B … Escape goes to the page” |\n\nThe same review also disposed of 33 earlier findings. Their status at this commit is as follows.\n\n| Finding | Severity | Status | Evidence at `bbd7564` | Reverting test |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| C2-1 · Paused call order | B | **fixed** | `controller.ts:647,650,709,890` | `review2:54,77,99` replacement and rejected updates while paused |\n| C2-2 · Category identity | B | **fixed** for focus and category eviction | `interaction.ts:1648,1728` | `review2:121,136` B survives and A moves to B; `review4:199,219` pin and dismissal eviction |\n| C2-3 · Empty-window recovery | B | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:572,906,1520,1748` | `review2:152,172,184` empty window, Reset, Resume; `final-pin:26` |\n| C2-4 · Frozen native range | B | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:808` updates bounds and ordinal before the text guard. | `review2:203` one-point chart gains a second point |\n| C2-5 · Retention and caller rows | M | **fixed** for the reported sequence | `controller.ts:1483,1495` retains displayed, pending, and held owners. | `final-review.test.ts:103,113` bounded paused store and exact displayed caller row |\n| C2-6 · Native adjustment intent | M | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:879,962` resolves absolute ordinals and suppresses duplicate delivery. | `review2:370` Home then assistive set; `final-pin:348` input-only and change-only |\n| C2-7 · Keyboard information loss | M | **fixed** | `focus.ts:133,147,159` reads all rows and qualifies the incomplete total once. | `focus-reading:14` ten series with one gap |\n| C2-8 · Single-pointer pan and range | M | **partly fixed** | `interaction.ts:1017,1257,1526` retains the tap anchor and provides pan buttons. Two-click range selection is the **known in-progress item**. | `final-partials:19` tap 80 then Zoom in gives `[40,90]`; **none** for exact two-click endpoints |\n| C2-9 · Unattainable zoom minimum | M | **fixed** | `focus.ts:432,478,486` | `focus2:60,73,131` two positions, large offset, category bars |\n| C2-10 · Gesture ownership | M | **fixed** for capture, pair ownership, and cancellation | `interaction.ts:1197,1269,1307,1357` | `review2:419` Escape during drag; `review4:146` cancelled pinch. **None** identified for a third finger replacing an owner. |\n| C2-11 · Stale scatter pin | M | **fixed** for disappearance or hiding of the pinned scatter ref | `interaction.ts:1688,1691` | `review5:125,135` y exclusion and new neighbours; `final-pin:222` hide A |\n| C2-12 · Clipped or transformed tip | M | **partly fixed** | `mapping.ts:47,89`; `interaction.ts:765`; `chart.ts:196` | `review5:152` scaled bar; `final-pin:279,315` clipped card and painted centres |\n| C2-13 · Narrow readout | M | **partly fixed** | `interaction.ts:483,1084`; `tooltip.ts:356`; `css.ts:193` | `final-hold:139,156` routes to strip; **none** for a wholly clipped strip |\n| C2-14 · Arcless donut focus | M | **fixed** for the reported mixed donut | `interaction.ts:698,779`; `css.ts:246,255` | `review2:497` zero first slice and inset plot ring |\n| C2-15 · Open-table layout | M | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:1492`; `css.ts:293` | `review2:518` fixed card and pager; `review5:188` shrink and grow text |\n| C2-16 · Page-count announcement | M | **fixed** at the DOM level | `table.ts:163` sets live delivery before changing the count. | `review2:536` append adds a page |\n| C2-17 · Focus on removal or reorder | M | **partly fixed** | `toolbar.ts:146`, `table.ts:152`, `interaction.ts:536` cover toolbar, pager, and teardown. `interaction.ts:264,1848` can remove a focused list or tooltip row before handoff. | `review2:558,567`; `final-partials:35` compact with toolbar or jump field focused; **none** for the two row cases |\n| C2-18 · Jump-to grammar | M | **partly fixed** | `interaction.ts:339,363,1417` rejects ordinary trailing text but fails on some strings the chart itself formats. | `focus-placement:183,195,204`; `final-partials:53,66` unit and wall time; **none** for the locale counterexamples below |\n| C2-19 · Per-string language | M | **partly fixed** | `interaction.ts:248,1465,1627` tags several surfaces. The proxy still shares one language across name, role, and value. Tooltip missing values and jump errors have no corresponding language write at `tooltip.ts:149`, `table.ts:184`. | `final-partials:95,104,122` proxy, cells, donut; **none** for mixed proxy languages or jump errors |\n| C2-20 · Shared axis unit | M | **fixed** | `axes.ts:265,280,303` | `focus2:138` changing only the second series unit |\n| C2-21 · Accessibility evidence | M | **partly fixed** | Positive pin-button AX check at `final-pin:126`. Rehearsal remains open at `acceptance/report.md:247`. A9 remains a placeholder at `apps/docs/pages/conformance.md:3`. | `final-pin:115` named AX buttons; **none** for the published A9 table and its test references |\n| C2-22 · Contrast swatch dash | m | **fixed** | `swatch.ts:103`; `css.ts:220` | `review2:616` contrast swatch uses the line’s dash |\n| C3-1 · Narrowed scatter hangs | B | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:890,897` bounds global traversal and exits narrowed mode on a series change. | `review3:27`; `final-pin:348` A0 B1 A2 B3 A4 |\n| C3-2 · Table covers right toolbar | B | **fixed** | `figure.ts:157`; `interaction.ts:1447,1492`; `css.ts:293` | `review3:52,73` right disclosure hit-test and shrinking card |\n| C3-3 · Speed-dependent hover | M | **partly fixed** | `css.ts:179`; `interaction.ts:1084,1778`. The remaining timing error is across frames. | `review6:58,75,86`; `final-hold:119,172` |\n| C3-4 · Focused text churn | M | **partly fixed** | `interaction.ts:813`; `focus.ts:206` | `final-pin:81`; `review5:239` all-mode category slide; **none** for single mode |\n| C3-5 · Replacement splits focus and text | M | **fixed** for epoch replacement | `interaction.ts:1703,1748,1799` | **none** identified that replaces the epoch and checks text, ring, and Enter together. `final-pin:26` exercises same-epoch reset. |\n| C3-6 · Compact or too-small transition | M | **partly fixed** | `interaction.ts:1815,1844` clears the hold. Tooltip focus can disappear before teardown records it at `:1848`. | `final-hold:247` compact round trip; `review4:96,111` proxy handoff; **none** for a focused pin row |\n| C3-7 · Zoom-in widens | M | **fixed** | `focus.ts:432,451`; `interaction.ts:1328` | `focus-placement:166,172`; `final-partials:134` spread below minimum |\n| C3-8 · Unavailable slider | M | **fixed** | `interaction.ts:572,796,1611,1748` | `review4:54,72` loading and all-hidden recovery; `final-pin:26` |\n| C3-9 · Unusable touch targets | M | **partly fixed** | `css.ts:202`; `tooltip.ts:125,220,356`. Visible ordinary buttons work; clipping and incomplete paging still remove actions. | `review5:42,67`; `final-pin:182` exact secondary strip tap |\n| C3-10 · Gesture work crosses owners | M | **fixed** for the reported sequences | `interaction.ts:512,1188,1269,1880` | `review4:146,177` cancelled pinch and release outside a nonzoomable plot |\n| C3-11 · Bar cue repeats at 33 | M | **fixed** by the F9 amendment | `02-product-spec.md:102`; `scene/bars.ts:18` | `type-matrix:550` thirty-two distinct colour/pattern combinations |\n\n## Decision 0004 rule by rule\n\n| Rule | Implementing code | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 · Datum anchor | `interaction.ts:742`; `focus.ts:381` | **Pass for drawable marks.** Placement uses the complete union at x, independent of pointer position and narrowed mode. If every anchor is null, it invents the plot centre at `interaction.ts:745`. Revision 3 gives no anchor for an all-gap x. |\n| 2 · Candidate order and validity | `placement.ts:116,131,144`; `interaction.ts:755` | **Partial.** Both side orders and hole-first containment work. Validity depends on an incomplete set of clips, controls, and focus extents. |\n| 3 · Transparent hovered content | `css.ts:179,186`; `interaction.ts:483,1131,1222` | **Pass for mouse activation.** A rested Q3 readout over Q4 still sends the click to Q4. An empty physical pick selects nothing. |\n| 3b · Rest, hull, and invalidation | `interaction.ts:1080,1135,1383,1768,1803`; `placement.ts:209` | **Partial.** The 250 ms clock, 2 viewport-pixel radius, convex hull, and same-move exit work on a stable frame. Rest can span an intervening datum or presentation. Escape from `held` retains the displayed target instead of immediately re-picking the stationary pointer. |\n| 4 · Pin, rows, and keyboard | `interaction.ts:717,832,1231,1298`; `tooltip.ts:125`; `css.ts:202` | **Partial.** Mouse activation, row buttons, and keyboard placement work in the ordinary case. Touch release can select the wrong datum. Keyboard takeover also releases a pin on an endpoint key that moves nowhere. |\n| 5 · Reserved readout | `controller.ts:1313`; `interaction.ts:156,1825`; `tooltip.ts:323`; `css.ts:190` | **Partial.** Three modes and two CSS line heights exist. The controller can choose the wrong mode from an estimate, and retaining one row in the DOM does not make it visible or operable. |\n| 6 · Drop rows, then minimize overlap | `tooltip.ts:295,309`; `placement.ts:169` | **Partial.** The outer box is capped against the supplied rectangle. Clipped contents can pass the fit test, and fallback does not always find the least-overlap position. |\n| 7 · Escape | `interaction.ts:443,940,1351` | **Partial.** The tested visible pin → single-series mode → dialog sequence takes three Escapes. Hidden pins and multiple chart owners break the general guarantee. |\n| 8 · One datum per pin and dismissal | `interaction.ts:1247,1685,1703`; `pointer.ts:30,38` | **Partial.** Disabled tooltips cannot pin. Epoch replacement drops pins. Scatter pin survival checks its ref; aligned survival and scatter dismissal do not consistently do so. |\n| 9 · Accessible, persistent row buttons | `tooltip.ts:72,113,125,153,220` | **Partial.** Ordinary pinned rows have accessible names and reuse their node. Reformatting, reordering during a press, or switching presentation can still lose the action or focus. |\n| 10 · Coordinate mapping | `mapping.ts:31,47,65,81`; `chart.ts:196` | **Partial.** Interaction uses fractional per-axis transforms. Measurement retains the known exception, clip traversal is incomplete, and the limitation documented in `mapping.ts:7` is missing from spec §3.8. |\n| Part 2 · Bounds, value, and four text-write reasons | `interaction.ts:791,839,962,975,1257,1742`; `focus.ts:196` | **Partial.** Bounds and numeric value track the frame. Navigation, assistive adjustment, changed values, eviction, and refocus have write paths. Single-series category renumbering also triggers a write. |\n\n**State transitions.** These are the actual transitions, including the handlers outside `reconcile`.\n\n| Starting state | Transitions at `bbd7564` |\n|---|---|\n| `none` | Mouse move → `hover(target or null)`. Proxy focus → `keyboard`. Activation with a ref and enabled presentation → `pinned`. Table opening and clearing → `none`. `interaction.ts:975,1075,1231,1437` |\n| `keyboard` | Navigation or adjustment → `keyboard`. Mouse move → `hover`. Activation → `pinned` or unpinned `hover`. Blur → a fresh `hover` if a pointer is stored, otherwise `none`. Escape dismisses content while retaining keyboard state. `interaction.ts:832,962,991,1351` |\n| `hover` | Move → new `hover`, or → `held` after qualifying rest. Leave → `keyboard` or `none`. Activation → `pinned` where available. Keyboard takeover → `keyboard`. Commit re-picks a stored pointer. `interaction.ts:633,1075,1135,1778` |\n| `held` | Inside the hull → `held`. Exit → fresh `hover` on that move. Click → fresh `pinned` or empty pick. Leave → idle. Key navigation → `keyboard`. Changed geometry → re-pick. Escape → dismissed `hover` with the **old** target. Rebuild → `none`. `interaction.ts:1088,1231,1365,1768,1844` |\n| `pinned` | Moves and leave retain the pin. Another plot activation replaces or ends it. Outside press, disappearance, or unavailable presentation → `hover` or idle. Navigation/refocus → `keyboard`. Visible Escape → dismissed `hover`. Opening the table or clearing → `none`. Drag and pinch can hide content **without changing this state**. `interaction.ts:832,1079,1121,1292,1314,1357,1757` |\n\n## New defects\n\nThese are concrete counterexamples beyond the two items already in progress. **Node** means I exercised the production calculation or lookup. **Trace** means I followed the committed event and DOM code.\n\n| Severity | Event sequence and wrong result | Smallest fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| B · Wrong activation | **Trace.** Touch down 1 px inside A’s band, lift 2 px away inside B before 500 ms, with no intervening move event. `pointerup` selects A from the last stored sample. A separate keyboard case is focus A → hover B → Enter. Enter calls `takeover` and selects B while the range still describes A. `interaction.ts:934,1104,1202` | Use the release event for tap displacement and picking. Enter/Space should select the ref the focused range describes. |\n| B · Pin follows a different datum | **Node + trace.** Pin aligned A at x=1, then hide A with the keyboard legend while B remains. The committed lookup gave A ordinal `-1`, primary B, and rows `[B]`. `stillPinned` installs B as the pin. Even a same-frame redraw can replace a deliberately narrowed secondary ref with the primary. Pause preserves the displayed frame; Resume runs the same faulty reconciliation against the buffered frame. `interaction.ts:1243,1697,1758`; `controller.ts:709,890` | Validate the saved ref’s membership and visibility. Keep that exact ref while rebuilding the listed rows; end the pin when it leaves. |\n| B · An invisible pin traps interaction | **Trace.** Pin a numeric point → start a drag → move more than 4 px → Escape → move over another point. Drag start hides the tooltip, Escape only calls `endDrag`, and subsequent moves return because `shown` is still `pinned`. Another Escape can close the dialog while the chart retains its pin. A touch pinch with no committed zoom, followed by a mouse move, reaches the same state. A failed placement can also leave `pinned` with nothing visible. `interaction.ts:1079,1121,1314,1357`; `tooltip.ts:316` | Explicitly suspend or end the pin on gesture start, reconcile and present on every exit, and handle Escape from pin state independently of `tooltip.visible`. |\n| B · Hidden rows pass the fit test | **Trace.** Clip a tall floating chart to a 60 px-high visible band with room beside its active mark, then pin eight series. `maxHeight` and `overflow:hidden` cap the container *before* measurement. Its box can fit while later buttons and the paging action are cut off. In a strip, a long title or first row can fill both lines before `+N more`. A wholly clipped strip still reports its full DOM rectangle. `tooltip.ts:279,295,310,356`; `css.ts:184,193,213` | Check intrinsic content overflow and the actual visible strip intersection. Drop rows until the title, one value, and any required paging target are physically available. |\n| B · Wrong visible region or covered control | **Trace.** Clip the plot’s stage to a narrow band, or mount in a shadow root inside a clipping card. The floating tooltip is a sibling of the stage, and `parentElement` traversal stops at the shadow boundary. A tip wider than the visible plot can be approved. An overlapping page control outside the figure is absent from the obstacle list. Even for a chart control, shifting flush to its border can cover its 3 px external focus outline. `figure.ts:157,160`; `mapping.ts:89`; `interaction.ts:755,765`; `css.ts:280` | Intersect the displayed plot’s composed clipping chain with the tooltip’s chain. Include overlapping controls and their painted focus extents. |\n| M · Rest clock survives a different datum | **Trace.** At 0 ms hover A. At 100 ms a redraw puts B under the stationary pointer. At 230 ms restore A. At 260 ms move along A’s corridor over B. The saved rest still starts at 0, so A holds after only 30 ms of continuous rest. Conversely, a stationary pointer newly over B can rest there for 300 ms and have no qualifying B rest. A 0.25 px anchor or rectangle change also passes `sameRect`. `interaction.ts:319,1084,1778,1829` | Restart the rest on a committed pick or presentation change using a clock comparable to event timestamps. Invalidate held geometry at layout precision. On Escape, update the physical pick separately from suppressing the dismissed content. |\n| M · Dismissal belongs to the sampled group | **Node + trace.** Dismiss scatter A, then append 15 coincident B rows. The group count was 16, its eight sampled refs were all B, and `matchesIdentity` returned false. A reopens under a stationary pointer. In the reverse order, pin A, append B, then Escape: dismissal can be recorded for B because B is now first. `pointer.ts:34,41`; `interaction.ts:1365` | Save the chosen ref on Escape and check its actual displayed membership independently of the eight tooltip rows. |\n| M · Some scatter rows cannot be selected | **Node.** I interleaved twelve near-coincident points with distant-y points in x order. The production pick counted **12**. `groupRefs` returned **8** because it stopped at the first nonmember in each direction. Paging at offset eight then returns the first model again. `focus.ts:175,180`; `interaction.ts:668` | Enumerate members by the lookup’s actual coincidence predicate. Use that enumeration for paging. |\n| M · A pressed or focused row moves or disappears | **Trace.** Pin A near the top so its tooltip is below. Press A’s row, append a later coincident B, then release. B is inserted above A, so down and up can hit different buttons. Changing a formatted x title replaces an aligned button even with the same ref. Resizing floating → strip destroys it outright. In a shadow root, document capture can also mistake a pin-row press for an outside press because `event.target` is the host. `tooltip.ts:72,84,248,257`; `interaction.ts:1298,1829` | Key by semantic identity, preserve focus across presentation changes, and defer reordering an active press or complete it against its captured ref. Determine inside presses from the composed event path. |\n| M · Unrequested focused-text rewrite | **Node + trace.** Narrow to Q3, value 3, in Q1–Q4. Append Q5 with `keep:4`. The semantic keys differed and the texts were `y, Q3, 3. Point 3 of 4.` and `y, Q3, 3. Point 2 of 4.` No reader action, value change, eviction of Q3, or refocus occurred. `focus.ts:206`; `interaction.ts:813,1721` | Compare the stable category identity and its spoken values. Keep its remapped numeric index solely for range synchronization. |\n| M · Reserving a strip can remove a readable plot | **Node, supplied host dimensions.** With a 112 px unstripped plot, a 30 px initial estimate, and a real 98 px strip, the controller committed `readoutMode='strip'`, `layout.kind='too-small'`. Rule 5 requires the readable plot with no readout. `controller.ts:1316,1325,1355` | Measure the strip’s own line height before deciding, or retry with `none` when reservation takes the plot below L8. |\n| M · Fallback needlessly covers more of the mark | **Node.** In a 100×100 visible region, active box `(28,28,44,44)`, and 55×55 tip, fallback chose `(22.5,0)` with **1,188 px²** overlap. `(0,0)` on the same side is legal and covers **729 px²**. `placement.ts:179` evaluates just one free-axis position per side. | Score the free-axis bounds and obstacle boundaries as well as the centered position. I read “overlaps the active box least” as applying to legal positions on the candidate side. |\n| M · Slice focus, jump input, and language | **Trace:** focus the second all-zero slice and redraw with a changed list signature. `replaceChildren` removes the focused button. **Node:** the chart’s own Arabic negative `؜-١٬٢٣٤٫٥ ms` returned `null`; its German date `31. Mai 2026` failed both parse paths. **Trace:** switching between translated `pointAll` and built-in `pointOf` changes the text immediately, but the proxy language is assigned only on commit. `interaction.ts:264,363,873,1417,1627` | Reconcile list entries by slice key. Accept the field’s formatted values, including localized signs and dates. Update value language with each reading and give independently worded labels their own language-bearing element. |\n\n## Claims not confirmed\n\n- The author’s typecheck, 207 core tests, browser totals, old-bundle failures, and scratch mutation runs are reported for a shared tree. I did not independently reproduce those runs or the explanation for the canvas memory failure. My six-suite Git-blob run ended with:\n\n  ```text\n  ℹ tests 123\n  ℹ suites 56\n  ℹ pass 123\n  ℹ fail 0\n  ℹ cancelled 0\n  ℹ skipped 0\n  ℹ todo 0\n  ℹ duration_ms 1140.874117\n  ```\n\n- Several tests establish less than their titles suggest. The resize test computes and discards its expected datum. The dense sweep checks only the title and allows several ordinals of error. The narrow-strip test counts DOM entries. The pressed-row test fixes the domains and adds an unrelated row. The scale and eight-area-marker tests skip canvas. `final-hold:216,367`; `final-pin:104,208,317,377`.\n- The ordinary modal test establishes one Escape per action for its listener order. Each chart installs its own window-capture listener. With chart A pinned and chart B keyboard-focused, registration order can give B’s Escape to A. An earlier application window-capture handler can also act before the chart spends the key. `interaction.ts:437,1351`. Revision 3 does not specify arbitration between two active charts. It also leaves keyboard takeover of a pin underspecified; I would preserve a pin on a key that leaves the reader at the same datum.\n- The author’s general claims about fresh tap coordinates, Enter using the keyboard datum, preserving the chosen pin ref, complete overflow access, and clearing every hold on presentation change are contradicted by the paths above. The tests establish positive Chrome AX button names for the floating fixture. Speech, magnifier behavior, Firefox/WebKit behavior, and the five A3 rehearsals remain unverified. The earlier palette-document correction also remains open at `docs/decisions/0003-default-palette.md:171`. No public contract change is required for the demonstrated state transitions.\n\n**Release acceptance verdict: hold the sign-off run.** The implementation blockers are release-coordinate and keyboard activation, pin and dismissal identity, gesture/Escape recovery, rest invalidation, clipping and least-overlap placement, readable strip sizing, complete and stable pin-row actions, focused-category text stability, slice-focus handoff, and localized jump/language handling. The two-click range control and near-unity measurement correction remain the two already-tracked items. Add regressions for the uncovered cases, especially epoch replacement and independent keyboard-ring placement. A3 rehearsal and the A9 conformance table remain separate release-evidence obligations."}}
